WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.707
Question fourteen. Highlight: the string Hello; “standard A S C I I”; “one byte per character”.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:11.926
Useful: five characters times one byte = five bytes.

00:00:11.926 --> 00:00:16.145
Useless: what Hello means — does not change storage.

00:00:16.145 --> 00:00:18.417
Option A. Five bytes — keep.

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:23.203
Option B. Six bytes: often wrongly adds a terminator — cut.

00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:27.828
Option C. Ten bytes: maybe counting two bytes each — cut.

00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:32.696
Option D. Forty bytes: maybe counting bits without ÷8 — cut.

00:00:32.696 --> 00:00:36.266
Five characters, one byte each — five bytes.

00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:39.024
Therefore the correct answer is A.
